333 | \n334 |     return tags\n```\n\n\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:default_tags`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:default_tags`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:default_tags`.\n```\n247 | def default_tags(estimator) -> Tags:\n248 |     \"\"\"Get the default tags for an estimator.\n249 | \n250 |     This ignores any ``__sklearn_tags__`` method that the estimator may have.\n251 | \n252 |     If the estimator is a classifier or a regressor, ``target_tags.required``\n253 |     will be set to ``True``, otherwise it will be set to ``False``.\n254 | \n255 |     ``transformer_tags`` will be set to :class:`~.sklearn.utils. TransformerTags` if the\n256 |     estimator has a ``transform`` or ``fit_transform`` method, otherwise it will be set\n257 |     to ``None``.\n258 | \n259 |     ``classifier_tags`` will be set to :class:`~.sklearn.utils.ClassifierTags` if the\n260 |     estimator is a classifier, otherwise it will be set to ``None``.\n261 |     a classifier, otherwise it will be set to ``None``.\n262 | \n263 |     ``regressor_tags`` will be set to :class:`~.sklearn.utils.RegressorTags` if the\n264 |     estimator is a regressor, otherwise it will be set to ``None``.\n265 | \n266 |     Parameters\n267 |     ----------\n268 |     estimator : estimator object\n269 |         The estimator for which to get the default tags.\n270 | \n271 |     Returns\n272 |     -------\n273 |     tags : Tags\n274 |         The default tags for the estimator.\n275 |     \"\"\"\n276 |     est_is_classifier = getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None) == \"classifier\"\n277 |     est_is_regressor = getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None) == \"regressor\"\n278 |     target_required = est_is_classifier or est_is_regressor\n279 | \n280 |     return Tags(\n281 |         estimator_type=getattr(estimator, \"_estimator_type\", None),\n282 |         target_tags=TargetTags(required=target_required),\n283 |       