se.OutlierMixin`.\",\n330 |             category=FutureWarning,\n331 |         )\n332 |         tags = default_tags(estimator)\n333 | \n334 |     return tags\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on the provided supplemental context and the search results, we can manually verify the line numbers and contents of the functions `_find_tags_provider`, `_to_new_tags`, and `_to_old_tags` in `sklearn/utils/_tags.py`.\n\nLet's explicitly search for the contents of these functions using the correct line numbers.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=line_nums>\n[296, 457, 519]\n</parameter>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>\nsklearn/utils/_tags.py\n</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"sklearn/utils/_tags.py:line 296, 457, 519\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound code snippet in file `sklearn/utils/_tags.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code context including sklearn/utils/_tags.py:line 296, 457, 519.\n```\n\n```\n\nFound code snippet in file `sklearn/utils/_tags.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code context including sklearn/utils/_tags.py:line 296, 457, 519.\n```\n\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`.\nSource: Retrieved code context including sklearn/utils/_tags.py:line 296, 457, 519.\n```\n293 | def get_tags(estimator) -> Tags:\n294 |     \"\"\"Get estimator tags.\n295 | \n296 |     :class:`~sklearn.BaseEstimator` provides the estimator tags machinery.\n297 |     However, if an estimator does not inherit from this base class, we should\n298 |     fall-back to the default tags.\n299 | \n300 |     For scikit-learn built-in estimators, we should still rely on\n301 |     `self.__sklearn_tags__()`. `get_tags(est)` should be used when we\n302 |     are not sure where `est` comes from: typically\n303 |     `get_tags(self.estimator)` where `self` is a meta-estimator, or in\n304 |     the common checks.\n305 | \n306