quested feature description**: `rewrite(abs)` should call `rewrite(Abs)`\n- **Behavior without this feature**: `sign(x).rewrite(abs)` returns `sign(x)`\n- **Expected behavior with the feature**: `sign(x).rewrite(abs)` should return `Piecewise((0, Eq(x, 0)), (x/Abs(x), True))`\n- **Additional context**: `rewrite(x)` dispatches to `_eval_rewrite_as_x`; the method is named `_eval_rewrite_as_Abs` because `Abs` is the class name. People usually use `abs` which dispatches to `Abs`.\n\nModules mentioned in the context:\n- `sympy/core/expr.py`\n- `sympy/core/numbers.py`\n- `sympy/core/function.py`\n- `sympy/core/basic.py`\n- `sympy/printing/str.py`\n- `sympy/core/add.py`\n- `sympy/core/evalf.py`\n- `sympy/core/mul.py`\n- `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py`\n\nBased on the issue description, let's explore the dependency structure around the `sign` function and `rewrite` method to locate the relevant areas for the feature implementation.\n\n<function=explore_tree_structure>\n<parameter=start_entities>['sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py:sign']</parameter>\n<parameter=direction>downstream</parameter>\n<parameter=traversal_depth>3</parameter>\n<parameter=dependency_type_filter>['invokes', 'imports']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "explore_tree_structure", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nsympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py:sign\n"}, {"content": "The observation shows that the `sign` function in `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py` does not directly show its dependencies or invocations. Let's search for the `rewrite` method in the same file to see if it provides more context.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>[\"rewrite\"]</parameter>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"rewrite\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound file `sympy/unify/rewrite.py`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `rewrite`.\n```\n 1 | \"\"\" Functions to support rewriting of SymPy expressions \"\"\"\n 2 | \n 3 | from sympy.core.expr import Expr\n 4 | from sympy.assumptions import ask\n 5 | from sympy.strategies.tools import subs\n 6 | from sympy.unify.usympy import rebuild, unify\n 7 | \n 8 | def rewriterule(source, target, variables=(), condition=None, assume=None):\n 9 |     \"\"\" Rewrite rule.\n10 | \n11 |     Transform expressions that match source into expressions that match target\n12 |     treating all ``variables`` as wilds.\n13 | \n14 |     Examples\n15 |     ========\n16 | \n17 |     >>> from sympy.abc import w, x, y, z\n18 |     >>> from sympy.unify.rewrite import rewriterule\n19 |     >>> from sympy import default_sort_key\n20 |     >>> rl = rewriterule(x + y, x**y, [x, y])\n21 |     >>> sorted(rl(z + 3), key=default_sort_key)\n22 |     [3**z, z**3]\n23 | \n24 |     Use ``condition`` to specify additional requirements.  Inputs are taken in\n25 |     the same order as is found in variables.\n26 | \n27 |     >>> rl = rewriterule(x + y, x**y, [x, y], lambda x, y: x.is_integer)\n28 |     >>> list(rl(z + 3))\n29 |     [3**z]\n30 | \n31 |     Use ``assume`` to specify additional requirements using new assumptions.\n32 | \n33 |     >>> from sympy.assumptions import Q\n34 |     >>> rl = rewriterule(x + y, x**y, [x, y], assume=Q.integer(x))\n35 |     >>> list(rl(z + 3))\n36 |     [3**z]\n37 | \n38 |     Assumptions for the local context are provided at rule runtime\n39 | \n40 |     >>> list(rl(w + z, Q.integer(z)))\n41 |     [z**w]\n42 |     \"\"\"\n43 | \n44 |     def rewrite_rl(expr, assumptions=True):\n45 |         for match in unify(source, expr, {}, variables=variables):\n46 |             if (condition and\n47 |                 not condition(*[match.get(var, var) for var in variables])):\n48 |                 continue\n49 |             if (assume and not ask(assume.xreplace(match), assumptions)):\n50 |                 continue\n51 |             expr2 = subs(match)(target)\n52 |             if isinstance(expr2, Expr):\n53 |                 expr2 = rebuild(expr2)\n54 |             yield expr2\n55 |     return rewrite_rl\n56 | \n```\n\nFound function `sympy/series/gruntz.py:rewrite`.\nFound function `sympy/core/basic.py:Basic.rewrite`.\nFound function `sympy/combinatorics/fp_groups.py:rewrite`.\nFound function `sympy/functions/elementary/piecewise.py:Piecewise._eval_rewrite_as_KroneckerDelta.rewrite`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `rewrite`.\nHint: Use more detailed query to get the full content of some if needed.\n"}, {"content": "The search indicates that the `rewrite` method is defined in `sympy/core/basic.py`. Let's retrieve the complete implementation of this method to understand where the special casing for `abs` to `Abs` should be added.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['sympy/core/basic.py:Basic.rewrite']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sympy/core/basic.py:Basic.rewrite`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sympy/core/basic.py:Basic.rewrite`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sympy/core/basic.py:Basic.rewrite`.\n```\n1996 | def rewrite(self, *args, deep=True, **hints):\n1997 |         \"\"\"\n1998 |         Rewrite *self* using a defined rule.\n1999 | \n2000 |         Rewriting transforms an expression to another, which is mathematically\n2001 |         equivalent but structurally different. For example you can rewrite\n2002 |         trigonometric functions as complex exponentials or combinatorial\n2003 |         functions as gamma function.\n2004 | \n2005 |         This method takes a *pattern* and a *rule* as positional arguments.\n2006 |         *pattern* is optional parameter which defines the types of expressions\n2007 |         that will be transformed. If it is not passed, all possible expressions\n2008 |         will be rewritten. *rule* defines how the expression will be rewritten.\n2009 | \n2010 |         Parameters\n2011 |         ==========\n2012 | \n2013 |         args : Expr\n2014 |             A *rule*, or *pattern* and *rule*.\n2015 |             - *pattern* is a type or an iterable of types.\n2016 |             - *rule* can be any object.\n2017 | \n2018 |         deep : bool, optional\n2019 |             If ``True``, subexpressions are recursively transformed. Default is\n2020 |             ``True``.\n2021 | \n2022 |         Examples\n2023 |         ========\n2024 | \n2025 |         If *pattern* is unspecified, all possible expressions are transformed.\n2026 | \n2027 |         >>> from sympy import cos, sin, exp, I\n2028 |         >>> from sympy.abc import x\n2029 |         >>> expr = cos(x) + I*sin(x)\n2030 |         >>> expr.rewrite(exp)\n2031 |         exp(I*x)\n2032 | \n2033 |         Pattern can be a type or an iterable of types.\n2034 | \n2035 |         >>> expr.rewrite(sin, exp)\n2036 |         exp(I*x)/2 + cos(x) - exp(-I*x)/2\n2037 |         >>> expr.rewrite([cos,], exp)\n2038 |         exp(I*x)/2 + I*sin(x) + exp(-I*x)/2\n2039 |         >>> expr.rewrite([cos, sin], exp)\n2040 |         exp(I*x)\n2041 | \n2042 |         Rewriting behavior can be implemented by defining ``_eval_rewrite()``\n2043 |         method.\n2044 | \n2045 |         >>> from sympy import Expr, sqrt, pi\n2046 |         >>> class MySin(Expr):\n2047 |         ...     def _eval_rewrite(self, rule, args, **hints):\n2048 |         ...         x, = args\n2049 |         ...         if rule == cos:\n2050 |         ...             return cos(pi/2 - x, evaluate=False)\n2051 |         ...         if rule == sqrt:\n2052 |         ...             return sqrt(1 - cos(x)**2)\n2053 |         >>> MySin(MySin(x)).rewrite(cos)\n2054 |         cos(-cos(-x + pi/2) + pi/2)\n2055 |         >>> MySin(x).rewrite(sqrt)\n2056 |         sqrt(1 - cos(x)**2)\n2057 | \n2058 |         Defining ``_eval_rewrite_as_[...]()`` method is supported for backwards\n2059 |         compatibility reason. This may be removed in the future and using it is\n2060 |         discouraged.\n2061 | \n2062 |         >>> class MySin(Expr):\n2063 |         ...     def _eval_rewrite_as_cos(self, *args, **hints):\n2064 |         ...         x, = args\n2065 |         ...         return cos(pi/2 - x, evaluate=False)\n2066 |         >>> MySin(x).rewrite(cos)\n2067 |         cos(-x + pi/2)\n2068 | \n2069 |         \"\"\"\n2070 |         if not args:\n2071 |             return self\n2072 | \n2073 |         hints.update(deep=deep)\n2074 | \n2075 |         pattern = args[:-1]\n2076 |         rule = args[-1]\n2077 | \n2078 |         # support old design by _eval_rewrite_as_[...] method\n2079 |         if isinstance(rule, str):\n2080 |             method = \"_eval_rewrite_as_%s\" % rule\n2081 |         elif hasattr(rule, \"__name__\"):\n2082 |             # rule is class or function\n2083 |             clsname = rule.__name__\n2084 |             method = \"_eval_rewrite_as_%s\" % clsname\n2085 |         else:\n2086 |             # rule is instance\n2087 |             clsname = rule.__class__.__name__\n2088 |             method = \"_eval_rewrite_as_%s\" % clsname\n2089 | \n2090 |         if pattern:\n2091 |             if iterable(pattern[0]):\n2092 |                 pattern = pattern[0]\n2093 |             pattern = tuple(p for p in pattern if self.has(p))\n2094 |             if not pattern:\n2095 |                 return self\n2096 |         # hereafter, empty pattern is interpreted as all pattern.\n2097 | \n2098 |         return self._rewrite(pattern, rule, method, **hints)\n```\n"}, {"content": "The `rewrite` method in `sympy/core/basic.py` uses a method naming convention `_eval_rewrite_as_<rule>` to determine how to rewrite an expression. Given the issue, we need to ensure that `rewrite(abs)` calls `rewrite(Abs)`.\n\nNext, let's locate the `sign` function and check its `_eval_rewrite_as_Abs` method to understand where the feature should be integrated.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py:sign._eval_rewrite_as_Abs']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py:sign._eval_rewrite_as_Abs`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py:sign._eval_rewrite_as_Abs`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py:sign._eval_rewrite_as_Abs`.\n```\n439 | def _eval_rewrite_as_Abs(self, arg, **kwargs):\n440 |         return Piecewise((0, Eq(arg, 0)), (arg / Abs(arg), True))\n```\n"}, {"content": "We have found the `_eval_rewrite_as_Abs` method in `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py`. This method handles the rewriting of the `sign` function using `Abs`. Now, we need to ensure that `rewrite(abs)` calls this method by adding a special case for `abs` in the `rewrite` method of `Basic` class.\n\nTo do this, we should modify the `sympy/core/basic.py` file to add a check for `abs` and call `_eval_rewrite_as_Abs` if `abs` is passed.\n\nLet's also look at the `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py` file to see if there are any other relevant methods or functions that might need modification.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py`...\n### Search Result:\nFound file `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sympy/functions/elementary/complexes.py`.\n```\n   1 | from typing import Tuple as tTuple\n   2 | \n   3 | from sympy.core import S, Add, Mul, sympify, Symbol, Dummy, Basic\n   4 | from sympy.core.expr import Expr\n   5 | from sympy.core.exprtools import factor_terms\n   6 | from sympy.core.function import (DefinedFunction, Derivative, ArgumentIndexError,\n   7 |     AppliedUndef, expand_mul, PoleError)\n   8 | from sympy.core.logic import fuzzy_not, fuzzy_or\n   9 | from sympy.core.numbers import pi, I, oo\n  10 | from sympy.core.power import Pow\n  11 | from sympy.core.relational import Eq\n  12 | from sympy.functions.elementary.miscellaneous import sqrt\n  13 | from sympy.functions.elementary.piecewise import Piecewise\n  14 | \n  15 | ###############################################################################\n  16 | ######################### REAL and IMAGINARY PARTS ############################\n  17 | ###############################################################################\n  18 | \n  19 | \n  20 | class re(DefinedFunction):\n  21 |     \"\"\"\n  22 |     Returns real part of expression. This function performs only\n  23 |     elementary analysis and so it will fail to decompose properly\n  24 |     more complicated expressions. If completely simplified result\n  25 |     is needed then use ``Basic.as_real_imag()`` or perform complex\n  26 |     expansion on instance of this function.\n  27 | \n  28 |     Examples\n  29 |     ========\n  30 | \n  31 |     >>> from sympy import re, im, I, E, symbols\n  32 |     >>> x, y = symbols('x y', real=True)\n  33 |     >>> re(2*E)\n  34 |     2*E\n  35 |     >>> re(2*I + 17)\n  36 |     17\n  37 |     >>> re(2*I)\n  38 |     0\n  39 |     >>> re(im(x) + x*I + 2)\n  40 |     2\n  41 |     >>> re(5 + I + 2)\n  42 |     7\n  43 | \n  44 |     Parameters\n  45 |     ==========\n  46 | \n  47 |     arg : Expr\n  48 |         Real or complex expression.\n  49 | \n  50 |     Returns\n  51 |     =======\n  52 | \n  53 |     expr : Expr\n  54 |         Real part of expression.\n  55 | \n  56 |     See Also\n  57 |     ========\n  58 | \n  59 |     im\n  60 |     \"\"\"\n  61 | \n  62 |     args: tTuple[Expr]\n  63 | \n  64 |     is_extended_real = True\n  65 |     unbranched = True  # implicitly works on the projection to C\n  66 |     _singularities = True  # non-holomorphic\n  67 | \n  68 |     @classmethod\n  69 |     def eval(cls, arg):\n  70 |         if arg is S.NaN:\n  71 |             return S.NaN\n  72 |         elif arg is S.ComplexInfinity:\n  73 |             return S.NaN\n  74 |         elif arg.is_extended_real:\n  75 |             return arg\n  76 |         elif arg.is_imaginary or (I*arg).is_extended_real:\n  77 |             return S.Zero\n  78 |         elif arg.is_Matrix:\n  79 |             return arg.as_real_imag()[0]\n  80 |         elif arg.is_Function and isinstance(arg, conjugate):\n  81 |             return re(arg.args[0])\n  82 |         else:\n  83 | \n  84 |             included, reverted, excluded = [], [], []\n  85 |             args = Add.make_args(arg)\n  86 |             for term in args:\n  87 |                 coeff = term.as_coefficient(I)\n  88 | \n  89 |                 if coeff is not None:\n  90 |                     if not coeff.is_extended_real:\n  91 |                         reverted.append(coeff)\n  92 |                 elif not term.has(I) and term.is_extended_real:\n  93 |                     excluded.append(term)\n  94 |                 else:\n  95 |                     # Try to do some advanced expansion.  If\n  96 |                     # impossible, don't try to do re(arg) again\n  97 |                     # (because this is what we are trying to do now).\n  98 |                     real_imag = term.as_real_imag(ignore=arg)\n  99 |                     if real_imag:\n 100 |                         excluded.append(real_imag[0])\n 101 |